        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is the Sole TT8 treadmill good?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On its published figures, yes, for heavy users and runners who want decline. Sole lists a 4.0 HP motor, a 22 by 60-inch deck, 12 mph, 15 incline and 6 decline levels, a 400 lb rating, 3-inch rollers and a lifetime frame and motor warranty. Independent coverage of the current touchscreen version is thin, and we have not tested it.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Sole TT8 discontinued?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sole has not said so. Its US store still lists the TT8 at $2,899.99, but it was marked sold out on 5 November 2026, as it was on 13 October. We do not know when stock will return. If you need a treadmill now, the in-stock Sole F85 is the closest alternative.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does the Sole TT8 have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sole’s warranty block for the current TT8 gives lifetime on the frame and motor, three years each on the deck, electronics and wear parts, and one year on labour. Older versions carried a lifetime deck, five years of parts and two of labour, so reviews describing those terms are out of date.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Sole TT8 have decline?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. Sole lists the grade as -6 to 15 levels, driven by two incline motors, and it is the only current Sole treadmill with decline. For deeper incline with the same -6% decline, the NordicTrack X16 and X24 go to 40%.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Sole TT8 vs F85: what is the difference?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Both have a 22 by 60-inch running surface and a 15.6-inch touchscreen. The TT8 adds decline, a 4.0 HP motor against 3.5 HP and a 400 lb rating against 350 lb, but does not fold. On 5 November 2026 the F85 was $2,199.99 and in stock; the TT8 was listed at $2,899.99 and sold out.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Sole TT8 fold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. It is a non-folding treadmill measuring 81 by 38 by 66 inches and weighing 319 lb. If you need to fold the machine away, the Sole F85 and F80 fold.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
